{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And not gerah.</b> It is defective, and it is as though ולא יגר גרה. Or like ולא לו גרה. <b>And in their carcasses you shall not touch.</b> In order to eat from them, like בכל קודש לא תגע — from which we derive a warning against eating, and it is a doubling of a word. And the matter seems correct, for if it entered your mind that the warning concerns touching, why was he warned about eating?"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:43.412201890Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}